\\pi ).$ So $f(x)$ has no non-stationary critical points.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the critical points of $f(x)$ for $x\\in (0,2\\pi )$ are ${x}_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and ${x}_{2}=\\frac{5\\pi }{4}.$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\cdot \\frac{5\\pi }{4}=\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{16}.\n$$" 13194139534178 true] [17592186280665 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280666 13194139534178 true] [17592186280665 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280667 13194139534178 true] [17592186280665 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280668 13194139534178 true] [17592186280665 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280669 13194139534178 true] [17592186280665 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280670 13194139534178 true] [17592186280665 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534178 true] [17592186280665 1041 "selection" 13194139534178 true] [17592186280665 1104 #edb/ref 17592186280667 13194139534178 true] [17592186280665 1110 #uuid "4dea5912-59da-54f5-a993-0b791e756393" 13194139534178 true] [17592186280666 1034 "\\frac{4{\\pi }^{2}}{9}" 13194139534178 true] [17592186280666 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534178 true] [17592186280666 1111 #uuid "8a716a49-51ec-54e0-ae4e-94352d1c8d25" 13194139534178 true] [17592186280667 1034 "\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{16}" 13194139534178 true] [17592186280667 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534178 true] [17592186280667 1111 #uuid "a6d7a4ed-32b8-54d7-9197-4f0546245ca3" 13194139534178 true] [17592186280668 1034 "\\frac{7{\\pi }^{2}}{9}" 13194139534178 true] [17592186280668 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534178 true] [17592186280668 1111 #uuid "1600cac6-2d8b-56bd-afe7-4f137ba3fcf0" 13194139534178 true] [17592186280669 1034 "\\frac{21{\\pi }^{2}}{16}" 13194139534178 true] [17592186280669 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534178 true] [17592186280669 1111 #uuid "109c70b9-d380-527e-8bce-a2dfaa037768" 13194139534178 true] [17592186280670 1034 "\\frac{7{\\pi }^{2}}{16}" 13194139534178 true] [17592186280670 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534178 true] [17592186280670 1111 #uuid "e0ee478