 [17592186280711 1145 "A critical point of $f(x)$ is a point $x=c$ in the domain of $f$ such that either ${f}^{′}(c)=0$ or ${f}^{′}(c)$ does not exist.\n\nDifferentiating $f(x),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3}+9{x}^{2}+24x-11) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}+18x+24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to find the critical points:\n\n- First, we compute the points where ${f}^{′}(c)=0.$ We set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}+18x+24 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+6x+8 & =0 \\\\ (x+4)(x+2) & =0 \\\\ x & =-4,\\,-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ has stationary points at $x=-4$ and $x=-2.$\n\n- Second, we note that ${f}^{′}(x)$ exists for all values of $x$ in the domain of $f(x).$ So $f(x)$ has no non-stationary critical points.\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the critical points of $f(x)$ are $x=-4$ and $x=-2.$" 13194139534178 true] [17592186280712 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280713 13194139534178 true] [17592186280712 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534178 true] [17592186280712 1041 "field-1" 13194139534178 true] [17592186280712 1104 #edb/ref 17592186280713 13194139534178 true] [17592186280712 1110 #uuid "5a6531eb-b67a-5542-9e05-a69455577972" 13194139534178 true] [17592186280713 1034 "-4" 13194139534178 true] [17592186280713 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534178 true] [17592186280713 1111 #uuid "919dc54f-5cc5-52ba-abe2-ef8a234b0ec9" 13194139534178 true] [17592186280714 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280715 13194139534178 true] [17592186280714 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534178 true] [17592186280714 1041 "field-2" 13194139534178 true] [17592186280714 1104 #edb/ref 17592186280715 13194139534178 true] [17592186280714 1110 #uuid "61091b4e-5f84-58d2-b183-e89cbfab11ba" 13194139534178 true] [17592186280715 1034 "-2" 13194139534178 true] [17592186280715 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534178 true] [17592186280715 1111 #uuid "346db744-fd1a-56a4-9fb3-c6a9538fd256" 13194139534178 true] [