}]{e}^{x-1} \\\\  & =(x+1)^{2}(x+4){e}^{x-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to find the critical points:\n\n- First, we compute the points where ${f}^{′}(c)=0.$ We set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)^{2}(x+4){e}^{x-1} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${e}^{x-1}\\ne 0$ for all $x,$ we can divide this equation by ${e}^{x-1}$ and solve the resulting equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)^{2}(x+4) & =0 \\\\ x & =-4,\\,-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ has stationary points at $x=-4$ and $x=-1.$\n\n- Second, we note that ${f}^{′}(x)$ exists for all values of $x$ in the domain of $f(x).$ So $f(x)$ has no non-stationary critical points.\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the critical points of $f(x)$ are\n\n$$\nx=-4\\,\\text{and}\\,x=-1.\n$$" 13194139534178 true] [17592186280723 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280724 13194139534178 true] [17592186280723 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534178 true] [17592186280723 1041 "field-1" 13194139534178 true] [17592186280723 1104 #edb/ref 17592186280724 13194139534178 true] [17592186280723 1110 #uuid "6bc40150-6359-5379-bf14-bc3763ee9fd9" 13194139534178 true] [17592186280724 1034 "-4" 13194139534178 true] [17592186280724 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534178 true] [17592186280724 1111 #uuid "6365089c-ca2d-5190-84f6-7bb5774db6c5" 13194139534178 true] [17592186280725 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280726 13194139534178 true] [17592186280725 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534178 true] [17592186280725 1041 "field-2" 13194139534178 true] [17592186280725 1104 #edb/ref 17592186280726 13194139534178 true] [17592186280725 1110 #uuid "bd796db4-1258-57be-90fe-ae8a87711227" 13194139534178 true] [17592186280726 1034 "-1" 13194139534178 true] [17592186280726 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534178 true] [17592186280726 1111 #uuid "9f8aad47-7111-501c-a0e7-3e02ef73e2c0" 13194139534178 true] [17592186280727 1017 #edb/ref 17592186280728 13194139534178 true] [17592186280727 1017 #edb/ref 17592